Z||000000||My7Fieros||02-14-2001||01:50 PM||||Well I was changing out the temp sensor in my (always giving me a headache) Formula yesterday and when I pulled off the connector....CRUMBLE!!! EEK!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> What do I do? The actual connectors are still there, but the platic housing around it was crispy fried to a crackly crunch! I supose after 13 years in a high heat enviroment its gonna happen...but, what to do now? Thanx.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||11
