Z||000003||Phil||02-14-2001||05:40 PM||||Pep Boys has a whole big wall full of sensor connectors.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bob Englert||02-14-2001||08:20 PM||||AC Delco makes connectors with wires you can splice for almost all the applications you need, including the temp sensor.<P>If you need the 2 wire sensor let me know and I will see if I have one unopened and I will get the P/N for you.<P>When splicing in the new pigtail, be carefull to get the wires on the right connectors.  1 lead is for the gauge, the other is for the warning light.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000005||My7Fieros||02-15-2001||01:41 AM||||Thanx....<BR>Bob you've got mail.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||02-15-2001||01:48 AM||||Man, I thought you were talking about an electrical fire!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> <P>I have the same problem with most of my connectors... usually only snap off the locking tab, though.  Haven't had on fall off because of that yet...||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bob Englert||02-15-2001||09:58 AM||||The temp sensor pigtail on both of my recently purchased 87 GT's were completely missing, only the wires were stuck on the pins of the sensor.<P>The ACDelco P/N for the replacement pigtail is PT110.  Most auto parts stores that carry ACDelco parts should be able to get it for you.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||02-15-2001||02:31 PM||||ya, all the connectors in Fieros fry from the heat. When I replaced my ign module and induction coil in my distributor they both turned to plastic dust when I touched them.||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||02-15-2001||07:32 PM||||MotorMite ConnectTite line has the vast majority of GM electrical connectors. MotorMite parts are available thru nearly all parts stores.<P>Which temp sensor is it? The old style ECT sensor for the ECM is no longer made. (This is in the thermostat neck on the 4. don't know where on the 6.) If that's the one you broke replace the sensor and use Borg Warner brand. B-W is only a couple dollars more but comes with the connector you ned for the new sensor. If you get another brand you'll still need the connector and the 2 parts will cost more than B-W. And yes! the leads on this connector MUST be soldered for reliable operation.||||reg||1
